(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast Microprocessors and Microcontrollers, detailing internal architecture, memory organization, and system cost.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Microprocessors versus Microcontrollers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Microprocessor \(e.g., Intel Core i7, AMD Ryzen, ARM Cortex-A\):) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Silicon chip houses exclusively the Central Processing Unit \(ALU, Register) Tj
T*
(   File, Control Unit, and Cache\).) Tj
T*
(   - System Integration: RAM, ROM/Flash, I/O ports, timers, and interrupt controllers must be) Tj
T*
(   connected externally via address, data, and control buses on a motherboard.) Tj
T*
(   - Design Philosophy: Optimized for raw computing power, multi-tasking desktop/server computing,) Tj
T*
(   and intensive floating-point mathematical computations.) Tj
T*
(   - Cost & Footprint: Bulky printed circuit board layout, high power consumption \(watts to tens) Tj
T*
(   of watts\), high system bill of materials \(BOM\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Microcontroller \(e.g., 8051, Microchip PIC, AVR ATmega328P, ARM Cortex-M\):) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Complete 'computer-on-a-chip'. Integrates the CPU, internal RAM, program) Tj
T*
(   ROM/Flash, timers/counters, GPIO ports, ADC, DAC, and serial communication peripherals onto a) Tj
T*
(   single monolithic die.) Tj
T*
(   - Design Philosophy: Optimized for dedicated real-time control, low latency event handling,) Tj
T*
(   ultra-low power consumption \(milliwatts to microwatts\), and compact footprint.) Tj
T*
(   - Cost & Footprint: Minimal external components \(typically only a crystal and decoupling) Tj
T*
(   capacitors required\); extremely low unit cost \(.50 to .00\), ideal for embedded consumer) Tj
T*
(   appliances, medical devices, and automotive controllers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the internal architectural block diagram of the 8051 Microcontroller, covering CPU, ALU, RAM structure, and SFRs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Internal Architecture of the 8051 Microcontroller:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Architectural Blocks:) Tj
T*
(   - 8-bit Central Processing Unit \(CPU\) with Arithmetic Logic Unit \(ALU\) capable of 8-bit) Tj
T*
(   addition, subtraction, multiplication \(MUL AB\), division \(DIV AB\), and extensive Boolean) Tj
T*
(   bit-level manipulation.) Tj
T*
(   - Accumulator \(ACC / A register\) and Register B used for arithmetic and register operations.) Tj
T*
(   - Program Counter \(PC\): 16-bit register holding the address of the next instruction to fetch) Tj
T*
(   from 64 KB program space.) Tj
T*
(   - Data Pointer \(DPTR\): 16-bit register composed of DPH and DPL, used to address external data) Tj
T*
(   memory.) Tj
T*
(   - Program Status Word \(PSW\): Contains flags CY \(Carry\), AC \(Auxiliary Carry\), F0 \(User Flag\),) Tj
T*
(   RS1/RS0 \(Register Bank Select\), OV \(Overflow\), and P \(Parity\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Internal RAM Organization \(128 Bytes: 00H to 7FH\):) Tj
T*
(   - Banked Working Registers \(00H to 1FH, 32 bytes\): Divided into four 8-byte banks \(Bank 0, 1,) Tj
T*
(   2, 3\), each containing registers R0 to R7. Selected via PSW.3 \(RS0\) and PSW.4 \(RS1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Bit-Addressable RAM \(20H to 2FH, 16 bytes\): Contains 128 individual directly addressable bits) Tj
T*
(   \(bit addresses 00H to 7FH\).) Tj
T*
(   - General-Purpose Scratchpad RAM \(30H to 7FH, 80 bytes\): Used for variables, data buffering,) Tj
T*
(   and the hardware stack \(Stack Pointer SP defaults to 07H on reset, growing upward into 08H\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Special Function Registers \(SFRs: 80H to FFH\):) Tj
T*
(   - 21 dedicated control and status registers including Port registers \(P0, P1, P2, P3\), Timers) Tj
T*
(   \(TH0, TL0, TH1, TL1, TMOD, TCON\), Serial interface \(SBUF, SCON, PCON\), and Interrupt control) Tj
T*
(   \(IE, IP\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
