(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture of the ARM Cortex-M Processor family, detailing Programmer's model, NVIC, and pipeline.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   ARM Cortex-M Architecture and Real-Time Core:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Features:) Tj
T*
(   - 32-bit RISC processor core based on ARMv7-M / ARMv8-M architecture.) Tj
T*
(   - High instruction density achieved via Thumb-2 instruction set \(combines 16-bit and 32-bit) Tj
T*
(   instructions\).) Tj
T*
(   - Multi-stage pipeline \(3-stage in Cortex-M3/M4: Fetch, Decode, Execute\) with hardware divide) Tj
T*
(   and single-cycle 32x32 multiply.) Tj
T*
(   2. Programmer's Register Model:) Tj
T*
(   - 13 General-Purpose Registers: R0 to R12 \(R0-R7 low registers, R8-R12 high registers\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stack Pointer \(R13 / SP\): Dual banked into Main Stack Pointer \(MSP\) used by OS) Tj
T*
(   kernel/interrupts and Process Stack Pointer \(PSP\) used by application tasks.) Tj
T*
(   - Link Register \(R14 / LR\): Stores return address for subroutines and exception returns) Tj
T*
(   \(EXC_RETURN\).) Tj
T*
(   - Program Counter \(R15 / PC\): Holds current execution address.) Tj
T*
(   - Special Registers: xPSR \(Program Status Register\), PRIMASK, FAULTMASK, BASEPRI, and CONTROL.) Tj
T*
(   3. Nested Vectored Interrupt Controller \(NVIC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Tightly coupled to the CPU core for deterministic, ultra-low-latency interrupt response \(12) Tj
T*
(   clock cycles in Cortex-M3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hardware Vectoring: Vector table holds direct function pointer addresses of ISRs \(no software) Tj
T*
(   jump tables required\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hardware Stacking: Registers R0-R3, R12, LR, PC, and xPSR are automatically pushed onto stack) Tj
T*
(   by hardware during exception entry, and popped on exit.) Tj
T*
(   - Tail-Chaining: When an interrupt arrives while another ISR is completing, the core skips the) Tj
T*
(   unstacking/restacking sequence, vectoring to the pending ISR in only 6 clock cycles!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
