(   - Step 1: Hardware clears all SAR bits to 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Clock Cycle 1 \(Test MSB bit N-1\):) Tj
T*
(   SAR sets MSB = 1 \(Binary code: 100...0\).) Tj
T*
(   Internal DAC outputs Vdac = Vref / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Comparator inspects: Is Vin >= Vdac?) Tj
T*
(   * If Vin >= Vdac: Comparator output is HIGH. SAR keeps MSB = 1.) Tj
T*
(   * If Vin < Vdac: Comparator output is LOW. SAR resets MSB = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Clock Cycle 2 \(Test Next Bit N-2\):) Tj
T*
(   SAR sets bit N-2 = 1. Internal DAC evaluates new Vdac.) Tj
T*
(   Comparator tests Vin vs Vdac; SAR retains or resets bit N-2 based on result.) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration: The process repeats sequentially for all bits down to LSB \(bit 0\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Performance Characteristics:) Tj
T*
(   - Conversion Time: Exactly N clock cycles for an N-bit ADC regardless of analog input) Tj
T*
(   amplitude:) Tj
T*
(   t_conv = N / f_clk.) Tj
T*
(   - For a 12-bit SAR ADC clocked at 1 MHz, conversion completes in exactly 12 microseconds.) Tj
T*
(   - Achieves optimal compromise between speed, circuit area, power dissipation, and resolution \(8) Tj
T*
(   to 18 bits\).) Tj
