(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Flash \(Parallel\) ADC and Dual-Slope Integrating ADC, comparing conversion speed, complexity, and noise immunity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Analysis: Flash ADC versus Dual-Slope Integrating ADC:) Tj
T*
(   1. Flash \(Parallel\) ADC:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Uses a precision resistor divider ladder of 2^N matched resistors generating) Tj
T*
(   2^N - 1 reference voltage levels, connected to 2^N - 1 analog comparators in parallel.) Tj
T*
(   - Conversion Mechanism: Input voltage Vin is applied to all comparators simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(   Comparators below Vin output '1', while those above output '0', producing a 'Thermometer Code'.) Tj
T*
(   A digital priority encoder converts thermometer code into standard binary output.) Tj
T*
(   - Conversion Speed: Ultrafast! The entire conversion completes in ONE clock cycle \(~1 to 5) Tj
T*
(   nanoseconds, speeds up to several Gigasamples/sec\).) Tj
T*
(   - Drawback: Circuit complexity explodes exponentially: an 8-bit flash ADC requires 255) Tj
T*
(   comparators; a 10-bit requires 1023 comparators. High silicon area and heavy power consumption) Tj
T*
(   limit resolution to 6-8 bits.) Tj
T*
(   2. Dual-Slope Integrating ADC:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Op-amp integrator, comparator, precision clock counter, and electronic) Tj
T*
(   switches.) Tj
T*
(   - Conversion Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Phase 1 \(Run-Up\): Switch connects Vin to integrator for fixed time T1 = 2^k / f_clk.) Tj
T*
(   Integrator ramps down to voltage V_int = - \(Vin / RC\) * T1.) Tj
T*
(   * Phase 2 \(Run-Down\): Switch connects fixed negative reference -Vref. Integrator ramps upward) Tj
T*
(   with constant slope Vref / RC until output crosses zero. Counter measures time T2 = N / f_clk) Tj
T*
(   taken to return to zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Equating slopes: \(Vin / RC\) * T1 = \(Vref / RC\) * T2 => Vin = Vref * \(T2 / T1\) = Vref * \(N /) Tj
T*
(   2^k\).) Tj
T*
(   - Speed & Noise: Sluggish conversion \(thousands of clock cycles\), but integration completely) Tj
T*
(   cancels high-frequency noise and 50/60 Hz line hum! R and C values cancel out, providing) Tj
T*
(   extreme measurement precision \(6.5 digit digital multimeters\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
