(   [Problem Statement]: Explain R-2R Ladder Digital-to-Analog Converter \(DAC\), deriving output voltage using Thevenin equivalent circuits.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   R-2R Ladder Digital-to-Analog Converter \(DAC\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Consists of a repetitive ladder network requiring only two precision resistor values: R and) Tj
T*
(   2R.) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates the severe fabrication difficulty of binary-weighted DACs where resistor values) Tj
T*
(   range across powers of 2 \(e.g., 10 k, 20 k, 40 k, 80 k...\).) Tj
T*
(   - Each bit switch Di connects the bottom of its 2R resistor to either reference voltage Vref) Tj
T*
(   \(if bit = 1\) or Ground \(if bit = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Terminated at the far left by an extra 2R resistor to ground.) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof of Node Impedance Equivalence:) Tj
T*
(   - Inspecting the ladder from left to right:) Tj
T*
(   At the leftmost node: 2R in parallel with 2R = R.) Tj
T*
(   This equivalent resistance R is in series with ladder resistor R, forming R + R = 2R.) Tj
T*
(   At the next node, this 2R is again in parallel with branch 2R, yielding R!) Tj
T*
(   - Principle of Invariance: The driving-point resistance seen looking into any node toward the) Tj
T*
(   left is ALWAYS identically equal to R.) Tj
T*
(   3. Output Voltage Derivation via Superposition:) Tj
T*
(   - When bit N-1 \(MSB\) is 1 \(connected to Vref\) and all other bits are 0:) Tj
T*
(   The Thevenin voltage seen at the rightmost ladder output node is Vref / 2, with Thevenin) Tj
T*
(   resistance R.) Tj
T*
(   - When bit N-2 is 1 alone:) Tj
T*
(   The voltage produced at the output is Vref / 4.) Tj
T*
(   - When bit k is 1 alone:) Tj
T*
(   Vout_k = Vref / 2^\(N - k\).) Tj
T*
(   - By Superposition, the total output voltage Vout for an N-bit digital input [D_{N-1} D_{N-2}) Tj
T*
(   ... D0] is:) Tj
T*
(   Vout = Vref * Sum_{k=0}^{N-1} [ D_k * 2^{-\(N - k\)} ] = \(Vref / 2^N\) * Sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \(D_k *) Tj
T*
(   2^k\).) Tj
T*
(   - Connected to an inverting op-amp summing stage, the ladder delivers smooth, monotonic analog) Tj
T*
(   voltages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
