(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principle and operation of a Linear Variable Differential Transformer \(LVDT\) for position sensing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Linear Variable Differential Transformer \(LVDT\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Construction:) Tj
T*
(   - A non-contact inductive electromechanical transducer that translates rectilinear physical) Tj
T*
(   displacement into a proportional AC electrical signal.) Tj
T*
(   - Stator: Cylindrical hollow coil former housing three coaxial coils:) Tj
T*
(   * One central Primary Winding \(P\) energized with high-frequency AC excitation \(1 to 10 kHz, 3) Tj
T*
(   to 15 V RMS\).) Tj
T*
(   * Two identical Secondary Windings \(S1 and S2\) placed symmetrically on either side of the) Tj
T*
(   primary, connected in Series Opposition \(differential connection\).) Tj
T*
(   - Armature: A high-permeability cylindrical ferromagnetic soft iron core attached to the) Tj
T*
(   external object whose displacement is being measured, sliding axially inside the coil bore) Tj
T*
(   without physical contact.) Tj
T*
(   2. Operating Principle across Displacement:) Tj
T*
(   - Null Position \(Core Centered\):) Tj
T*
(   Flux linkages from primary to both secondaries are identical \(Phi1 = Phi2\).) Tj
T*
(   Induced secondary voltages are equal in magnitude and 180 degrees out of phase: E_s1 = E_s2.) Tj
T*
