(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Temperature Sensors: Compare Thermocouples, Resistance Temperature Detectors \(RTDs\), and Thermistors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Engineering of Temperature Transducers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Thermocouple:) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Seebeck Effect. When two dissimilar metals \(e.g., Chromel-Alumel [Type K],) Tj
T*
(   Iron-Constantan [Type J]\) are joined at two junctions held at different temperatures \(T_hot and) Tj
T*
(   T_cold\), a thermoelectric EMF is generated:) Tj
T*
(   V_emf = alpha * \(T_hot - T_cold\) + beta * \(T_hot - T_cold\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Temperature Range: Extremely wide \(-200 deg C to +1800 deg C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Self-powered \(generates voltage directly\), rugged, low cost, fast response.) Tj
T*
(   - Disadvantages: Low output voltage \(~microvolts/deg C\), non-linear, requires Cold Junction) Tj
T*
(   Compensation \(CJC\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Resistance Temperature Detector \(RTD\):) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Positive Temperature Coefficient \(PTC\) of high-purity metallic wire \(typically) Tj
T*
(   Platinum: PT100, PT1000\). Resistance increases linearly with temperature:) Tj
T*
(   R\(T\) = R0 * [ 1 + A*T + B*T^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Temperature Range: -200 deg C to +650 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Highly linear, highest accuracy and repeatability among all industrial) Tj
T*
(   temperature sensors \(international standard for metrology\).) Tj
T*
(   - Disadvantages: Requires excitation current source \(risk of self-heating error\), sluggish) Tj
T*
(   thermal response, lead wire resistance requires 3-wire/4-wire compensation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Thermistor \(NTC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Ceramic metal-oxide semiconductor exhibiting an exponential Negative Temperature) Tj
T*
(   Coefficient \(NTC\):) Tj
T*
(   R\(T\) = R0 * exp[ beta * \(1/T - 1/T0\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Temperature Range: -50 deg C to +150 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Ultra-high sensitivity \(~3-5% resistance change per deg C\), compact size, low) Tj
T*
(   cost.) Tj
T*
(   - Disadvantages: Highly non-linear \(Steinhart-Hart equation required for linearization\), narrow) Tj
T*
(   range.) Tj
T*
