(   1. Physical Layer:) Tj
T*
(   - A synchronous, multi-master, multi-slave, half-duplex, 2-wire serial bus developed by Philips) Tj
T*
(   \(NXP\).) Tj
T*
(   - Two bi-directional open-drain / open-collector signal lines:) Tj
T*
(   * SDA: Serial Data line.) Tj
T*
(   * SCL: Serial Clock line.) Tj
T*
(   - Both lines are pulled up to +Vdd \(e.g., +3.3 V or +5 V\) through external pull-up resistors) Tj
T*
(   \(typically 2.2 k to 4.7 kOhms\).) Tj
T*
(   - Bus is idle when both SDA and SCL are HIGH.) Tj
T*
(   2. Bus Signaling Conditions:) Tj
T*
(   - Data Validity Rule: SDA must remain strictly stable while SCL is HIGH. SDA is only permitted) Tj
T*
(   to change state when SCL is LOW.) Tj
T*
(   - START Condition: A HIGH-to-LOW transition on SDA while SCL remains HIGH. Initiates a) Tj
T*
(   transmission.) Tj
T*
(   - STOP Condition: A LOW-to-HIGH transition on SDA while SCL remains HIGH. Terminates) Tj
T*
(   transmission.) Tj
T*
(   3. Byte Transfer and Acknowledge \(ACK / NACK\):) Tj
T*
(   - Data is transferred in 8-bit bytes, Most Significant Bit \(MSB\) first.) Tj
T*
(   - Every byte is followed by a 9th clock pulse for Acknowledge:) Tj
T*
(   * The transmitter releases SDA \(allowing it to float HIGH\).) Tj
T*
(   * The receiver pulls SDA LOW during the 9th SCL HIGH pulse to signal ACK. If SDA remains HIGH,) Tj
T*
(   it signals NACK.) Tj
T*
(   4. Addressing Frame:) Tj
T*
(   - Following a START condition, master sends a 7-bit slave address followed by an 8th bit) Tj
T*
(   indicating Read \(1\) or Write \(0\).) Tj
T*
(   - The addressed slave responds with ACK, establishing the communication link.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
