BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the SPI \(Serial Peripheral Interface\) Protocol: Bus signals, clock polarity/phase \(CPOL, CPHA\), and daisy-chaining.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   SPI \(Serial Peripheral Interface\) Protocol Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Bus Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - A synchronous, four-wire, full-duplex, single-master serial communication interface developed) Tj
T*
(   by Motorola.) Tj
T*
(   - Four dedicated physical lines:) Tj
T*
(   * SCLK \(Serial Clock\): Driven exclusively by master.) Tj
T*
(   * MOSI \(Master-Out Slave-In\): Serial data sent from master to slave.) Tj
T*
(   * MISO \(Master-In Slave-Out\): Serial data sent from slave to master.) Tj
T*
(   * SS' / CS' \(Slave Select / Chip Select\): Active-low line driven by master to select a specific) Tj
T*
(   slave.) Tj
T*
(   2. Clock Modes \(CPOL and CPHA\):) Tj
T*
(   - Controlled by two configuration bits establishing four distinct modes \(SPI Mode 0, 1, 2, 3\):) Tj
T*
(   * CPOL \(Clock Polarity\): Defines base idle level of clock. CPOL = 0 means clock idles LOW; CPOL) Tj
T*
(   = 1 means clock idles HIGH.) Tj
T*
(   * CPHA \(Clock Phase\): Defines which clock edge captures data.) Tj
T*
(   - CPHA = 0: Data is captured on the first \(leading\) clock edge and changes on second edge.) Tj
T*
(   - CPHA = 1: Data is captured on the second \(trailing\) clock edge and changes on first edge.) Tj
T*
(   * Mode 0 \(CPOL=0, CPHA=0\) and Mode 3 \(CPOL=1, CPHA=1\) are the most pervasive.) Tj
T*
(   3. Multi-Slave Configurations:) Tj
T*
(   - Star \(Independent CS\) Topology: Master uses dedicated individual CS lines for each slave) Tj
T*
(   peripheral. Fast and simple.) Tj
T*
(   - Daisy-Chain Topology: Master connects MOSI to Slave 1, Slave 1 MISO to Slave 2 MOSI, and so) Tj
T*
ET

