(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the CAN \(Controller Area Network\) Protocol: Physical differential layer, arbitration, message frames, and fault confinement.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Controller Area Network \(CAN\) Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Layer and Differential Signaling:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed by Bosch for automotive and industrial systems operating in harsh electromagnetic) Tj
T*
(   environments.) Tj
T*
(   - Operates over a single twisted pair terminated at both ends by 120-Ohm resistors:) Tj
T*
(   * CAN_H \(CAN High\) and CAN_L \(CAN Low\).) Tj
T*
(   - Recessive Bit \('1'\): CAN_H = 2.5 V, CAN_L = 2.5 V \(Differential voltage Vdiff = 0 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dominant Bit \('0'\): CAN_H = 3.5 V, CAN_L = 1.5 V \(Differential voltage Vdiff = 2.0 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Wired-AND logic: A dominant '0' driven by ANY node overrides a recessive '1' on the bus.) Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Destructive Bitwise Arbitration:) Tj
T*
(   - CAN is a CSMA/CD+AMP \(Arbitration on Message Priority\) protocol.) Tj
T*
(   - When multiple nodes transmit simultaneously, each node reads the bus while transmitting its) Tj
T*
(   identifier bit-by-bit.) Tj
T*
(   - If a node transmits a recessive '1' but reads back a dominant '0', it recognizes that a) Tj
T*
(   higher-priority message is transmitting, immediately ceases transmission, and switches to) Tj
T*
(   receiver mode.) Tj
T*
(   - The highest priority message \(lowest binary identifier value\) wins arbitration with ZERO bit) Tj
T*
(   loss or latency.) Tj
T*
(   3. CAN Data Frame Fields:) Tj
T*
(   - SOF \(1 bit\), Identifier \(11-bit standard or 29-bit extended\), RTR \(Remote Transmission) Tj
T*
(   Request\), Control Field \(DLC: 4 bits, indicating 0 to 8 data bytes\), Data Field \(0-8 bytes\),) Tj
T*
(   CRC \(15 bits + delimiter\), ACK Field \(2 bits\), and End of Frame \(7 bits\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Error Handling and Fault Confinement:) Tj
T*
(   - Bit stuffing, 15-bit CRC, frame check, and ACK monitoring.) Tj
T*
(   - Error counters \(TEC, REC\) transition nodes between Error Active, Error Passive, and Bus-Off) Tj
T*
(   states to isolate faulty nodes automatically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
