(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Programmable Logic Controllers \(PLCs\): Hardware architecture, scan cycle, and basic Ladder Logic programming.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Programmable Logic Controller \(PLC\) Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Hardware Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Central Processing Unit \(CPU\): Industrial microprocessor executing the logic solver and) Tj
T*
(   real-time executive.) Tj
T*
(   - Memory: Retentive battery-backed RAM/Flash for user ladder program and I/O image tables.) Tj
T*
(   - Power Supply: Converts 230 V AC mains to regulated isolated 24 V DC bus.) Tj
T*
(   - Input Modules: Opto-isolated digital inputs \(24 V DC, 120 V AC\) and analog inputs \(4-20 mA,) Tj
T*
(   0-10 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Output Modules: Relay contact outputs, transistor \(sink/source\) outputs, and triac outputs) Tj
T*
(   driving industrial contactors, solenoid valves, and indicator lamps.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Cyclic Scan Process:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Input Scan\): Hardware reads physical input pins and copies their status into the) Tj
T*
(   Input Image Table memory.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Program Scan / Logic Execution\): CPU evaluates ladder rungs sequentially from) Tj
T*
(   top-to-bottom, left-to-right, solving Boolean logic based on image table data.) Tj
T*
