(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Variable Frequency Drives \(VFDs\): Power electronic stages, V/f control, and Space Vector PWM.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Variable Frequency Drives \(VFD\) for AC Induction Motor Speed Control:) Tj
T*
(   1. Power Electronic Circuit Stages:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1 \(Rectifier\): 3-phase diode bridge rectifier converts incoming fixed-frequency 400 V,) Tj
T*
(   50 Hz AC supply into raw unregulated DC voltage.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2 \(DC Bus Filter\): High-capacity electrolytic capacitor bank and DC choke smooth DC) Tj
T*
(   voltage \(Vdc approx 1.35 * V_line = 540 V DC\) and absorb regenerative energy.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3 \(Inverter\): 3-phase bridge inverter containing 6 Insulated Gate Bipolar Transistors) Tj
T*
(   \(IGBTs\) with anti-parallel freewheeling diodes.) Tj
T*
(   2. Constant V/f \(Volts-per-Hertz\) Control:) Tj
T*
(   - Operating Principle: Air-gap magnetic flux is proportional to V / f: Phi proportional to V /) Tj
T*
(   f.) Tj
T*
(   - To maintain rated flux and prevent magnetic saturation \(overheating\) or under-fluxing \(torque) Tj
T*
(   loss\), the inverter adjusts stator voltage proportionally with frequency from 0 Hz up to rated) Tj
T*
(   50 Hz \(V/f = Constant\).) Tj
T*
(   - Base Speed and Field Weakening: Above 50 Hz, supply voltage is clamped at maximum line) Tj
T*
(   voltage \(400 V\). Frequency increases further, causing flux and available torque to decrease) Tj
T*
(   \(Field-Weakening Constant Power region\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Space Vector PWM \(SVPWM\):) Tj
T*
(   - Advanced digital switching algorithm that models 3-phase inverter voltages as a rotating) Tj
T*
(   space vector inside a 2D hexagon partitioned into six 60-degree sectors.) Tj
T*
(   - Modulates two adjacent active switching vectors and zero vectors to synthesize the reference) Tj
T*
(   vector with minimal harmonic ripple, achieving 15.47% higher DC bus voltage utilization than) Tj
T*
(   conventional sinusoidal PWM.) Tj
T*
