T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Industrial 4-20 mA Analog Current Loop Systems:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operating Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - A sensor transmitter converts a physical process variable \(e.g., pressure 0 to 100 bar\) into) Tj
T*
(   a proportional DC current ranging from 4 mA to 20 mA transmitted over a two-wire copper cable.) Tj
T*
(   - Process Mapping:) Tj
T*
(   * 0% Process Variable = 4.0 mA.) Tj
T*
(   * 50% Process Variable = 12.0 mA.) Tj
T*
(   * 100% Process Variable = 20.0 mA.) Tj
T*
(   2. Advantages over Voltage Signaling:) Tj
T*
(   - Total Immunity to Cable Resistance: In a series loop, current is identical at every point) Tj
T*
(   regardless of wire length or resistance. Voltage drops along long cables do NOT degrade) Tj
T*
