(   1. Physical Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - A fine metallic foil grid bonded to a flexible backing substrate attached to a mechanical) Tj
T*
(   structural member.) Tj
T*
(   - When strained, mechanical elongation increases length L and decreases cross-sectional area A) Tj
T*
(   \(via Poisson's ratio nu\), changing electrical resistance:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-R / R = GF * epsilon, where GF is Gauge Factor \(~2.0 for foil\) and epsilon = Delta-L / L) Tj
T*
(   is mechanical strain.) Tj
T*
(   2. Quarter-Bridge Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   - Single strain gauge R1 = R + Delta-R placed in one arm; three fixed completion resistors R in) Tj
T*
(   remaining arms.) Tj
T*
(   - Output voltage: Vout = V_ex * [ \(Delta-R / R\) / \(4 + 2*\(Delta-R / R\)\) ] approx \(V_ex / 4\) *) Tj
T*
(   \(Delta-R / R\) = \(V_ex / 4\) * GF * epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   - Severe drawback: Highly sensitive to ambient temperature drift \(wire thermal expansion mimics) Tj
T*
(   mechanical strain\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Half-Bridge Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   - Uses two active strain gauges: Gauge 1 mounted on top surface \(in tension: +Delta-R\), Gauge 2) Tj
T*
(   on bottom surface \(in compression: -Delta-R\).) Tj
T*
(   - Output voltage: Vout = \(V_ex / 2\) * \(Delta-R / R\) = \(V_ex / 2\) * GF * epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   - Double sensitivity; achieves complete automatic temperature compensation since thermal) Tj
T*
(   resistance changes in both arms cancel!) Tj
T*
(   4. Full-Bridge Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   - Uses four active strain gauges \(two in tension, two in compression\) in all four bridge arms.) Tj
T*
(   - Output voltage: Vout = V_ex * \(Delta-R / R\) = V_ex * GF * epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   - Four times the sensitivity of a quarter bridge, with complete temperature and lead-wire) Tj
T*
(   compensation.) Tj
T*
