(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Optocouplers and Solid-State Relays \(SSRs\) used for industrial Galvanic Isolation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Galvanic Isolation: Optocouplers and Solid-State Relays:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Industrial Ground Loop and Surge Threat:) Tj
T*
(   - High-power industrial actuators \(motors, contactors\) create violent inductive voltage spikes) Tj
T*
(   and circulating ground loop currents.) Tj
T*
(   - Connecting sensitive 3.3 V / 5 V microcontroller logic directly to 230 V / 400 V plant) Tj
T*
(   circuitry would cause instantaneous destruction.) Tj
T*
(   2. Optocoupler \(Opto-Isolator\):) Tj
T*
(   - Components: An infrared Light Emitting Diode \(Gallium Arsenide\) optically coupled across a) Tj
T*
(   transparent dielectric insulation barrier to a silicon phototransistor in a light-tight) Tj
T*
(   package.) Tj
T*
(   - Electrical isolation barrier withstands 2,500 V to 5,000 V RMS breakdown voltages.) Tj
T*
(   - An electrical logic HIGH energizes the LED, illuminating the phototransistor base and) Tj
T*
(   switching it ON, passing the signal with complete physical electrical isolation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Solid-State Relays \(SSRs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Electronic non-mechanical switching device replacing electromagnetic relays.) Tj
T*
(   - Uses an optocoupler driving back-to-back thyristors \(SCRs\) or a TRIAC for AC loads, or power) Tj
T*
(   MOSFETs for DC loads.) Tj
T*
(   - Features Zero-Voltage Crossing Switching: Turn-on occurs strictly when AC voltage passes) Tj
T*
(   through zero, eliminating inductive switching arcs, acoustic noise, and electromagnetic) Tj
T*
(   interference \(EMI\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 23:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Analog-to-Digital Conversion Errors: Quantization error, Integral Non-Linearity \(INL\), and Differential Non-Linearity \(DNL\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   ADC Performance Metrics and Error Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Quantization Error and Signal-to-Noise Ratio:) Tj
T*
(   - Quantization is the continuous-to-discrete rounding process.) Tj
T*
(   - Quantization uncertainty is fundamentally bounded within +- 1/2 LSB.) Tj
T*
(   - For a full-scale sinusoidal input, the theoretical maximum Signal-to-Quantization-Noise Ratio) Tj
T*
(   \(SQNR\) is given by Bennett's formula:) Tj
T*
(   SQNR = 6.02 * N + 1.76 dB \(where N is the number of ADC bits\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Differential Non-Linearity \(DNL\):) Tj
T*
(   - The deviation of an individual actual analog code step width from the ideal step width of 1) Tj
T*
(   LSB:) Tj
T*
(   DNL = [ \(V_{k+1} - V_k\) - 1 LSB ] / 1 LSB.) Tj
T*
(   - DNL = 0 means perfect 1 LSB step width.) Tj
T*
(   - If DNL < -1 LSB, the ADC suffers from Missing Codes \(a binary output code can never be) Tj
T*
(   produced\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Integral Non-Linearity \(INL\):) Tj
T*
(   - The maximum deviation of the actual ADC transfer characteristic from a reference straight) Tj
T*
(   line \(best-fit or end-point\):) Tj
T*
(   INL = [ V_actual\(k\) - V_ideal\(k\) ] / 1 LSB.) Tj
T*
(   - Quantifies overall non-linear distortion across the full dynamic range.) Tj
T*
(   4. Effective Number of Bits \(ENOB\):) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
