/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Modbus Serial Communication Frame formats: Modbus RTU vs Modbus ASCII.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Modbus Serial Communication Protocols \(RTU vs ASCII\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Modbus Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - A master-slave industrial query-response protocol. A single master initiates transactions) Tj
T*
(   with up to 247 slaves.) Tj
T*
(   2. Modbus RTU \(Remote Terminal Unit\):) Tj
T*
(   - Data Encoding: Compact binary format \(each 8-bit byte contains two 4-bit hexadecimal) Tj
T*
(   characters\).) Tj
T*
(   - Frame Delimitation: Silent intervals of at least 3.5 character times \(t3.5\) mark the start) Tj
T*
(   and end of a frame.) Tj
T*
(   - Frame Structure:) Tj
T*
(   * Slave Address \(1 byte: 1 to 247\).) Tj
T*
(   * Function Code \(1 byte: e.g., 03 Read Holding Registers, 06 Write Single Register\).) Tj
T*
(   * Data Payload \(N bytes\).) Tj
T*
(   * Error Check: 16-bit Cyclic Redundancy Check \(CRC-16\).) Tj
T*
(   - Performance: High data throughput, industry standard.) Tj
T*
(   3. Modbus ASCII:) Tj
T*
(   - Data Encoding: Every byte is transmitted as two human-readable ASCII characters \(0-9, A-F\).) Tj
T*
(   - Frame Delimitation: Explicit start character ':' \(colon, ASCII 3AH\) and end characters CR-LF) Tj
T*
(   \(0DH, 0AH\).) Tj
T*
(   - Error Check: Longitudinal Redundancy Check \(LRC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Performance: Exactly half the transmission efficiency of RTU, but tolerant of irregular) Tj
T*
(   transmission delays.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Ultrasonic Transducers and Time-of-Flight \(ToF\) distance measurement in robotics and process automation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ultrasonic Distance Measurement and Time-of-Flight:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Transducer Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Utilizes piezoelectric ceramic discs \(lead zirconate titanate, PZT\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inverse Piezoelectric Effect: An alternating electrical pulse train \(~40 kHz\) excites) Tj
T*
(   mechanical acoustic vibrations in the crystal, launching an ultrasonic acoustic wave pulse.) Tj
T*
(   - Direct Piezoelectric Effect: The returning reflected acoustic echo compresses the receiver) Tj
T*
(   crystal, generating a microvolt electrical signal.) Tj
T*
(   2. Time-of-Flight \(ToF\) Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - The wave travels from transducer to target and back to transducer \(total round-trip distance) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * D\).) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of sound in air: v = 331.3 * sqrt\( 1 + T / 273.15 \) m/s \(approx 343 m/s at 20 deg C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Distance equation:) Tj
T*
(   D = \(v * Delta-t\) / 2, where Delta-t is measured time-of-flight.) Tj
T*
(   3. Temperature Compensation:) Tj
T*
(   - Because sound speed shifts by ~0.6 m/s per deg C change in ambient temperature,) Tj
T*
(   high-precision industrial level transmitters integrate a temperature sensor to dynamically) Tj
T*
(   compensate sound speed v\(T\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
