(   Industry 4.0 and Cyber-Physical Automation Systems:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Industry 4.0 Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   - The Fourth Industrial Revolution transitions centralized automated manufacturing into) Tj
T*
(   decentralized, self-optimizing Cyber-Physical Systems \(CPS\).) Tj
T*
(   - Physical machines, sensors, and actuators are tightly coupled with cloud computing, digital) Tj
T*
(   twins, and big data analytics.) Tj
T*
(   2. Industrial Internet of Things \(IIoT\):) Tj
T*
(   - Edge devices \(smart sensors, intelligent drives\) connect securely to cloud platforms \(AWS) Tj
T*
(   IoT, Azure IoT\) via MQTT, CoAP, and AMQP protocols, enabling continuous real-time telemetry,) Tj
T*
(   predictive maintenance, and energy optimization.) Tj
T*
(   3. OPC Unified Architecture \(OPC UA - IEC 62541\):) Tj
T*
(   - A platform-independent, service-oriented open interoperability standard for industrial) Tj
T*
(   automation.) Tj
T*
(   - Replaces legacy COM/DCOM-dependent OPC with a modern, firewall-friendly TCP/IP protocol.) Tj
T*
(   - Comprehensive Information Modeling: Transmits rich semantic metadata alongside raw numerical) Tj
T*
(   variables \(e.g., units, scaling, calibration dates\).) Tj
T*
(   - Enterprise-Grade Security: End-to-end encryption, digital X.509 certificate authentication,) Tj
T*
(   and role-based access control, forming the universal communications backbone of Industry 4.0) Tj
T*
(   smart factories.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
